# Try the API from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client). Run it first: dotnet run --project src/RoomBooking.Api
@api = http://localhost:5080
@day = 2030-01-07

### RM-001: list rooms (only those for 8 people or more)
GET {{api}}/rooms?minCapacity=8

### RM-002: room details
GET {{api}}/rooms/atlas

### RM-003: availability of a room for a day
GET {{api}}/rooms/atlas/availability?date={{day}}

### BK-001: book a room
POST {{api}}/bookings
X-User: ana@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": "atlas",
  "title": "Sprint planning",
  "start": "{{day}}T10:00:00",
  "end": "{{day}}T11:00:00",
  "attendees": 4
}

### BK-002: same room, overlapping time -> 409 Conflict
POST {{api}}/bookings
X-User: luis@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": "atlas",
  "title": "1:1",
  "start": "{{day}}T10:30:00",
  "end": "{{day}}T11:30:00",
  "attendees": 2
}

### BK-006: my upcoming bookings
GET {{api}}/bookings/mine
X-User: ana@example.com

### BK-007: weekly booking for 4 weeks (weeks already taken are skipped and reported)
POST {{api}}/bookings/recurring
X-User: ana@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": "boreal",
  "title": "Team sync",
  "start": "{{day}}T09:00:00",
  "end": "{{day}}T10:00:00",
  "attendees": 6,
  "weeks": 4
}

### BK-005: cancel (replace the id with the one returned when booking)
POST {{api}}/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel
X-User: ana@example.com
